WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.400
Most food crops are contaminated
with fungal mycotoxins.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.534
Watch the video to find out how
much of a problem this may be.

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:16.577
"Ochratoxin and Breakfast Cereals,
Herbs, Spices, and Wine"

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.040
In France, exposure to dietary
contaminants was compared between

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:24.840
vegetarians and meat-eaters, and
the results showed that exposures

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.520
to persistent organic pollutants
like PCBs and dioxins

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.720
was dramatically lower among
those eating more plant-based

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:35.760
due to the non-consumption
of foods of animal origins—

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.240
though they did have
higher estimated exposure

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:43.120
to some mycotoxins, fungal
toxins present in moldy food.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.600
Now, there are lots types of mold
on the planet, and the vast majority

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.640
are harmless, but over the last
several years certain mold toxins,

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.880
such as aflatoxin and ochratoxin,

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:55.520
have been popping up
in breakfast cereals.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.640
Hundreds of samples were
taken off store shelves,

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:01.400
and about half were contaminated
with ochratoxin, for example;

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.600
but those were store
shelves in Pakistan.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.880
And Pakistan has a sub-tropical climate

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.200
with monsoons and ﬂash ﬂoods,
leading to fungal propagation.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.480
But then similar results

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:18.520
have popped up in Europe,
Serbia, Spain, Portugal.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:23.240
Then mycotoxins were discovered
in breakfast cereals in Canada.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.120
What about breakfast cereals
in the United States?

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.000
144 samples were collected,
and similar to other countries

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.680
about half were found
to contain ochratoxin,

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:36.120
but only about 7% exceeded
the maximum limit

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.200
established by the
European Commission.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.240
What is the signiﬁcance
of the finding of ochratoxin

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.960
in breakfast cereals
from the United States?

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:47.760
This was the largest study to date,
including nearly 500 samples

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:50.520
of cereal off store
shelves across the U.S.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:54.920
Overall detection rates were
about 40%, though only 16 violated

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:58.040
the European standards, all
the cereals with ochratoxin were

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:01.920
oat-based, making about
1 in 13 of the oat-based

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.800
breakfast cereal samples
tested being contaminated.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.320
Ochratoxin has become increasingly
regulated by many countries

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.520
to minimize chronic exposure.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:14.360
Here are the current regulations
for mycotoxins in cereal-based

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:18.520
baby foods worldwide, for example.
Some countries are very strict,

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:21.560
like in the European Union,
other countries less so,

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:25.840
and one country in particular
has no standards at all.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:29.840
Ochratoxin is not currently
regulated at all in the United States.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.360
What if you stick to organic products?

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.280
One might expect them to
actually be worse, owing to the fact

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.600
that fungicides are not
allowed in organic production.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.920
However, mycotoxin concentrations
are usually similar or even

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:45.720
reduced in organic compared
with conventional products.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.560
For example, in one of the
breakfast cereal studies,

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.880
researchers found similar
contamination,

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.000
and the same was
found for infant foods.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.240
It cannot be concluded
that one is better

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.200
than the other from a
mycotoxin perspective.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:00.520
Despite no use of fungicides,
organic systems appear generally

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:05.200
able to maintain mycotoxin
contamination at low levels.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.440
But how much is that saying
given how widespread it is?

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:11.920
How concerned should we be
about the public health effects

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.440
from long-term exposure
of this potent mycotoxin?

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:19.120
If you look at blood samples taken
from populations going back decades,

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.440
sometimes 100% of people turn
up positive for ochratoxin

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.400
circulating in their bloodstream.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.760
In some sense they are
unavoidable contaminants of food,

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:30.200
since the detection of
mycotoxins is not always easy

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:31.640
and they can remain hidden.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.640
And once foods have
become contaminated,

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.240
mycotoxins aren’t
destroyed by cooking.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:38.040
So, are there some foods we
should simply try to avoid

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.320
due to higher risk of contamination?

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:45.480
That’s exactly the question
I’m going to address next.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:49.000
Oats can be thought of as uniquely
nutritious, and one route

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.280
they improve human health is
by providing prebiotics

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:55.760
that increase the growth of
beneficial gut microbiota.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:57.920
Of course, there are oats
and then there are oats,

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:01.560
ranging from steel-cut oats, to
even better, intact oat groats

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:04.240
(their form before being cut),
all the way down

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:07.800
to highly processed cereals
such as Honey Nut Cheerios.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:10.960
Rolling crushes the grain
which may disrupt cell walls

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:15.000
and damage starch granules making
them more available for digestion,

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.520
which is bad, since we want
the starch to make it all

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.880
the way down to our colon to
feed our good gut bacteria.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:25.480
Grinding into oat flour to make
breakfast cereals is even worse.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:28.280
If you compare the blood sugar
and insulin responses, you can see

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:32.720
significantly lower spikes with
the more intact steel-cut oats.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:34.760
Okay, but what about ochratoxin?

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:36.960
The leading source
of dietary exposure of

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:41.240
this mold contaminant, but
they aren’t the only source.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:44.520
There’s a worldwide contamination
of food crops with mycotoxins,

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.280
with some experts
throwing around estimates

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:49.400
as high as 25% of the world’s crops.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.400
That statistic is attributed to
the Food and Agriculture Organization

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:56.440
of the United Nations, but it
turns out that statistic is bogus.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:01.760
It’s not 25%. Instead, it
may be more like 60 to 80%.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:04.280
The high occurrence is
likely explained by a combination

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:06.400
of the improved sensitivity
of testing methods

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:10.160
as well as the impact
of climate change.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.080
Spices have been found to have
some of the highest concentrations

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:16.720
of mycotoxins, but because they
are ingested in such small quantities,

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:19.160
they’re not considered
to be a signiﬁcant source.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:21.800
We can certainly do our
part to minimize risk, though.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:25.560
It is also the consumers’
responsibility to keep spices dry

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:28.920
after opening sealed
containers or packages.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:30.760
What about dried herbs?

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:35.400
Mycotoxins in plant-based dietary
supplements: the highest mycotoxin

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:38.920
concentrations were found in
milk thistle-based supplements.

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:41.560
It turns out wet and
humid weather is needed

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:44.560
during milk thistle harvest,
which evidently is why

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.760
they end up being so moldy.

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:49.720
Considering the fact that milk
thistle preparations are mainly used

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:53.000
by people who suﬀer from
a liver disease, such high intake

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:58.400
of compounds toxic to the
liver may present some concern.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.440
Wine sourced from the United
States also appears to have

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:02.440
particularly high levels.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:05.640
In fact, the single highest level
found to date around the world

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:09.840
is in American wine, but there’s
contamination in wine in general.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.760
In fact, some suggest that’s
why we see such consistent levels

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:17.400
in people’s blood—perhaps because lots
of people are regular wine drinkers.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:20.800
Ochratoxin is said to be a kidney
toxin with immunosuppressive,

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:24.000
birth defect-causing, and
carcinogenic properties.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:29.200
So, what about ochratoxin decontamination—
removing the toxin—in wine?

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:32.440
Now ideally, we’d try to prevent
the contamination in the first place,

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:35.920
but since this isn’t always
practical there is increased focus

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:39.440
on finding effective methods
of detoxification of mycotoxins

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:41.360
already present in foods.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:44.840
And that’s where yeast
comes in as a promising solution,

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:48.320
because the mycotoxins bind
to the yeast cell wall.

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:52.480
The thought is that you could strain
out the yeast, but another approach

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:54.840
would be to eat something
like nutritional yeast

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:58.240
to prevent the absorption.
It works in chickens.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:01.360
Give yeast along with aflatoxin
(another mycotoxin),

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:05.400
and you diminish the severity
of the resulting disease.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:09.320
But using something like nutritional
yeast as a binder depends on the

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:13.960
stability of the yeast-mycotoxin
bond throughout the digestive tract.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:18.600
We know yeasts can remove ochratoxin
in foods, but we didn’t have a clue

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:22.960
if it would work in the gut until 2016.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:27.440
Yeast was found to bind up to 44%
of the ochratoxin, but in actuality

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:29.240
it was probably closer
to only about a third

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:32.160
since some of the
bindings weren’t stable.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:35.320
So, if you’re trying to stay
under the maximum daily intake

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:38.720
and you drink a single glass
of wine, even if your bar snack

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:41.360
is popcorn seasoned
with nutritional yeast,

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:44.480
you’d still probably exceed
the tolerable intake.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:51.677
But what does that mean? How bad
is this stuff? We’ll find out next.

